  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 105 AM MDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nThe upper high will continue drifting east across southern NM on \nSaturday. Temps will remain hot areawide but with slightly higher \nhumidity and an uptick in high-based showers and storms over western \nNM. The high will drift even farther east into TX by Sunday with a \nmore noteworthy increase in moisture over western NM. An extension \nof the upper high westward into southern NM may choke off the better \nmoisture approaching from northern MX. Confidence is low on an \nactual uptick in the coverage of storms with heavy rainfall. Temps\nwill also remain hot, especially over eastern NM.\n\nMonday thru Wednesday are still looking like the more active days as \nthe upper high moves farther east toward the lower MS River Valley \nwhile an upper trough approaches from the west. A robust plume of \nmonsoon moisture will attempt to surge northward into NM. However, \nthis type of pattern has been advertised many times this season with \nvery little to show for it. Fortunately, temps will trend cooler but \nstill slightly above normal for central and eastern NM.",
